{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_deaeqcrrn2nyo7wb4ju6r6kbtfhfaobm3vk52ot5nl7vm5mhvzba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project compiles successfully and the tests pass for both the open hash table and the cuckoo hash table. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C cuckoo/open hash table library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n### `src/hash.rs`\n- `hash_by_power`: Polynomial rolling hash using `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` to mirror C's unsigned overflow.\n- `hash`, `alternative_hash`, `rehash`, `compare_keys`: thin wrappers matching the C semantics (using `Ord::cmp` for string compare).\n- Added private helpers `hash_str_by_power` / `hash_str` / `rehash_internal` that operate on `&str` (so they can be called from `find` with non-`'static` keys).\n\n### `src/log.rs`\n- `Logger::new`: Initializes the priority/prefix/suffix table for all four `LogType` variants, exactly matching the C `log_info_table`.\n- `insert_log`: Filters by priority (≤ stored) and prints `prefix + format + suffix`.\n- `change_log_priority`: Atomically swaps and returns the old priority.\n\n### `src/openhash.rs`\n- `new`: Allocates a vector of empty entries; debug-asserts the C invariants (size ≠ 0, ≠ POWER, ≠ REHASHER).\n- `query`: Linear probing using `rehash` to advance, returning the index of either the matching key or the first empty slot.\n- `insert`: Bumps `cur_size`, doubles and rehashes when above `LOAD_FACTOR`, then stores.\n- `find`: Returns the entry's data if present, `None` otherwise.\n- `free_open_hash_table`: Drops the array.\n\n### `src/cuckoohash.rs`\n- `new`: Allocates two vectors of size `initial_size/2` (matches the C halving in `create_cuckoo_hash_table`).\n- `insert`: Resizes when over the load factor, tries the first slot, then the second, then performs the eviction loop. Uses the `cur_marker` for cycle detection and falls back to `refill` + recursive insert.\n- `find`: Checks both arrays.\n- `resize`/`refill`/`recreate`: Reallocates the arrays and reinserts all entries (matching the C order: first array, then second).\n- The interface methods `get_first_entry`/`get_second_entry`/`try_to_store`/`swap_key_data_entry`/`free_cukoo_hash_table` are also implemented (with `unsafe` only inside the `&self -> &mut` accessors that the prescribed signatures forced).\n\nThe project compiles cleanly (only stylistic warnings) and passes a parity test against the C `test-cuckoohash.c` / `test-openhash.c` data sets."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":133,"cache_read_input_tokens":50677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":133,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7a99f85-deec-4516-926d-0ed8d84ac9e5","uuid":"2dd3dddf-346c-4f5f-868a-79392acd5166"}
